/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.1 The Iterative Design Loop and Refactoring) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Design Thinking is fundamentally non-linear and iterative. Testing does not mark the) Tj
T*
(conclusion of a project; it initiates the subsequent cycle of Refinement, Refactoring,) Tj
T*
(and Pivoting:) Tj
T*
(* Analyzing User Feedback: Separating superficial feature requests from fundamental) Tj
T*
(mental model mismatches. Prioritizing changes using the Impact vs. Effort matrix.) Tj
T*
(* Design Refactoring: Systematically restructuring design workflows, architecture,) Tj
T*
(and user interfaces without altering core intended functionality, improving) Tj
T*
(usability, speed, and elegance.) Tj
T*
(* Strategic Pivoting: When user testing reveals that initial core hypotheses were) Tj
T*
(fundamentally invalid, design teams pivot:) Tj
T*
(- Problem Pivot: User problem exists, but is different from what was originally assumed.) Tj
T*
(- Customer Segment Pivot: Product solves a genuine need, but for a completely different) Tj
T*
(user demographic.) Tj
T*
(- Feature Pivot: A single minor sub-feature of the product generates 90% of user) Tj
T*
(engagement and becomes the standalone core product.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.2 The NABC Value Proposition Model) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Developed by the Stanford Research Institute \(SRI\), the NABC framework structures) Tj
T*
(high-impact business and technical innovation proposals into four concise pillars:) Tj
T*
(* Need \(N\): An important, specific customer and market need. Quantified with real) Tj
T*
(user research and demographic statistics.) Tj
T*
(* Approach \(A\): The compelling, unique solution addressing the need. Includes) Tj
T*
(architecture, prototype evidence, and technical feasibility.) Tj
T*
(* Benefits \(B\): Quantifiable benefits per cost \(ROI, time savings, accuracy,) Tj
T*
(emotional delight\) delivered to the customer.) Tj
T*
(* Competition \(C\): Why the proposed solution is distinctly superior to current) Tj
T*
(alternatives, direct competitors, and the default status quo \('doing nothing'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.3 High-Impact Technical Presentations and Elevator Pitching) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* The Elevator Pitch: A concise, compelling 60-to-90 second spoken value proposition) Tj
T*
(structured as:) Tj
T*
(- The Hook: Relatable, startling problem statement.) Tj
T*
ET

