([CASE STUDY 1: The Instagram Pivot \(Burbn to Instagram\)]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: In 2010, Kevin Systrom and Mike Krieger launched 'Burbn', a complicated) Tj
T*
(HTML5 check-in app combining location check-ins, social points, and photo sharing.) Tj
T*
(Testing and User Analytics Insights:) Tj
T*
(User testing data revealed that users hated the complicated check-in and gaming) Tj
T*
(features, but LOVED sharing photos through vintage square filters.) Tj
T*
(Strategic Feature Pivot:) Tj
T*
(The team ruthlessly cut 90% of Burbn's features \(check-ins, games, complex profiles\).) Tj
T*
(Refocused solely on three core friction points: \(1\) Smartphone photos were blurry ->) Tj
T*
(solved with one-tap aesthetic filters, \(2\) Uploading took forever -> solved by starting) Tj
T*
(uploads while the user typed captions, \(3\) Sharing to multiple social networks was) Tj
T*
(painful -> solved with one-click multi-post.) Tj
T*
(Measurable Results: Rebranded as Instagram; gained 100,000 users in 24 hours, 10 million) Tj
T*
(in one year, and was acquired by Facebook for $1 Billion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([CASE STUDY 2: Formulating an NABC Model for a Hospital Telemetry App]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Proposal Title: CardioSense - AI-Powered Continuous Arrhythmia Telemetry.) Tj
T*
(The 4 NABC Pillars:) Tj
T*
(- Need: 30% of post-operative cardiac arrests in general hospital wards occur because) Tj
T*
(episodic 4-hour nurse vital checks fail to catch transient fatal arrhythmias.) Tj
T*
(- Approach: Ultra-low-power wearable chest patch transmitting single-lead ECG telemetry) Tj
T*
(via Bluetooth Low Energy \(BLE\) to an edge AI gateway that detects early warning signs 45) Tj
T*
(minutes before cardiac collapse.) Tj
T*
(- Benefits: Reduces post-op ICU transfers by 42%, saves an estimated $1.2M per hospital) Tj
T*
ET

